1
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:07,020
还剩一个饺子  谁要吃
Uh, one dumpling left. Who wants it?

2
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:09,540
或许你该让给怀孕的那位女士
Maybe you should offer it to the pregnant lady.

3
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:13,280
那位女士是...
And that would be...

4
00:00:15,130 --> 00:00:15,820
我啊  谢尔顿
Me, Sheldon.

5
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:17,500
我孕相多明显啊
I'm obviously pregnant.

6
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,400
因为你还没当面跟我说过
Well, you never said it to my face.

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,170
而我上一次想当然地认定一名女士怀孕时
And the last time I assumed a woman was pregnant,

8
00:00:21,170 --> 00:00:22,930
结果还挺糟糕的
it did not go over well.

9
00:00:22,930 --> 00:00:24,920
没错  我还在生你气呢
Yeah, I'm still mad at you.

10
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,700
你这酒鬼当时居然在喝白开水
You were drinking water instead of wine.

11
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,140
我这么想能怪我吗
What was I supposed to think?

12
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,440
谢尔顿说得对
Sheldon's right.

13
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:34,120
我永远不会问一个女士是不是怀孕
I would never ask a woman if she was pregnant,

14
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:37,210
除非是她告诉我  或是我看到有人类
unless she tells me or I see a human being

15
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:39,760
从她下面被拉出来
wiggling out of her.

16
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:42,310
谢尔顿  我怀孕了
Well, Sheldon, I'm pregnant.

17
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:44,790
恭喜你啊  怀孕多久了
Congratulations. How far along are you?

18
00:00:44,790 --> 00:00:46,070
大概三个月吧
About three months.

19
00:00:46,070 --> 00:00:48,580
才三个月吗
Only three?

20
00:00:49,130 --> 00:00:53,100
天啊  你肚子里是装的是几胞胎啊
Good gravy, how many babies are in there?

21
00:00:53,430 --> 00:00:54,880
够啦  咱们来聊一些
Okay, let's talk about something

22
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:58,470
不会让我的孕妻暴怒的话题吧
that won't infuriate my pregnant wife.

23
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:00,700
我读了一个有关大象的有趣知识
I read an interesting fact about elephants.

24
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:03,080
再换一个
Try again.

25
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:04,940
我想到啦
Oh, I've got something.

26
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:07,590
这周五我要接受电台访谈啦
I'm being interviewed on public radio this Friday.

27
00:01:07,590 --> 00:01:08,660
厉害  为什么呢
Oh, cool. How come?

28
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:10,480
大学希望物理系能获得
Uh, the university is trying to get more funding

29
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,510
更多研究资金
for the physics department,

30
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:13,560
所以就派我出马啊
so they want me to go out and talk it up.

31
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:16,210
真的吗  派你啊
Really? You?

32
00:01:18,230 --> 00:01:21,610
那他们还真是请对人了
Well, they picked the right person for the job.

33
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:23,120
真是谢谢啊
Thank you.

34
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:25,230
我觉得他信了
I think he bought it.

35
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,160
生

36
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,160
活

37
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,160
大

38
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,160
爆

39
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,160
炸

40
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,160
第十一季  第二集

41
00:01:52,770 --> 00:01:56,430
知名电台主持人  曾在本剧第7季第10集客串过

42
00:01:52,770 --> 00:01:55,380
欢迎收听《科学星期五》  我是艾拉·菲莱
Hi, I'm Ira Flatow, and this is Science Friday.

43
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:59,260
今天的嘉宾是物理学家莱纳德·霍夫斯塔德
Joining me today is my guest physicist, Dr. Leonard Hofstadter,

44
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:01,280
他要来跟我们聊他在加州理工
to talk about all of the exciting research

45
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,000
所做的那些激动人心的研究
they're doing at Cal Tech.

46
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,040
感谢贵节目给我这个机会...
Thank you for having me. Whoa...

47
00:02:05,770 --> 00:02:07,620
还是没办法习惯在耳机里听到自己的声音
Could never get used to hearing myself in headphones.

48
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:10,080
我的声音听起来真是这样吗
Is that really how I sound?

49
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,850
是的  真是
It is. It is.

50
00:02:11,850 --> 00:02:14,400
很高兴知道这点
That is good to know.

51
00:02:15,170 --> 00:02:16,640
我跟他说过他的声音很惹人厌
I told him his voice was annoying.

52
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:18,610
他就是不听
He didn't want to listen.

53
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:19,610
喂
Hey.

54
00:02:19,950 --> 00:02:21,710
难道你觉得不烦人吗
You're saying it's not?

55
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:23,010
就...
Just...

56
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:24,690
喂...
hey.

57
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:26,410
所以打从五年前
So, it has been five years

58
00:02:26,410 --> 00:02:28,500
希格斯玻色子被证实存在后
since the discovery of the Higgs boson--

59
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:31,030
您觉得下一个科学界大事是什么
what's the next big thing gonna be?

60
00:02:31,030 --> 00:02:32,310
这很难说啊
Wow, that's hard to say.

61
00:02:32,310 --> 00:02:33,670
有太多大事在发生了
There's so much going on.

62
00:02:33,670 --> 00:02:35,430
我们一直在搜集大量的数据
We've been collecting tons of data

63
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:38,240
而这数据有可能颠覆我们对宇宙的理解
that could revolutionize the way we understand the universe.

64
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:40,980
比如说  有个粒子叫超对称性夸克
For instance, there's a particle called a squark,

65
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:42,980
它能证明超对称性
which could prove supersymmetry.

66
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:44,770
有意思  那你们找到了吗
That is interesting. Have you found it?

67
00:02:44,770 --> 00:02:45,960
-什么  这个夸克吗  -对啊
- What, the squark? - Yes.

68
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,510
没  还没
No, no.

69
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,910
找到就是神作了
Wouldn't that be exciting?

70
00:02:51,650 --> 00:02:53,560
但我们也在试着找出超电子
But we're also looking for the selectron,

71
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:57,140
都是理论物理学家提出的物理模型中假想的一些粒子
基本没有切实的实验依据  很可能并不存在

72
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:55,100
胶微子与超中微子
the gluino and the neutralino.

73
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:57,140
-那找到那些了吗  -没有
- Well, and have you found that? - No.

74
00:02:58,560 --> 00:02:59,850
插个有趣小故事
Another fun sidenote--

75
00:02:59,850 --> 00:03:02,790
我有个高中同学名叫特丽莎·胶微子
I went to high school with a girl named Theresa Gluino,

76
00:03:02,790 --> 00:03:05,360
但要找到她并不需要花20亿
but it didn't cost $2 billion to find her.

77
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:08,180
她总躲在体育馆后面抽着烟
She was smoking behind the gym.

78
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:11,020
那你们发现了什么
So, what have you found?

79
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:12,640
其实什么都没发现
Uh, nothing, actually.

80
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:14,210
他可以说这话吗
Should he be saying that?

81
00:03:14,210 --> 00:03:15,820
应该不可以
Uh, probably not.

82
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:17,770
对啊  这可是公共电台
Yeah, this is public radio.

83
00:03:17,770 --> 00:03:21,810
难道他不知道"还有人"在听广播节目吗
Doesn't he realize that dozens of people might hear him?

84
00:03:22,510 --> 00:03:24,700
但我还是很有信心
But I remain confident.

85
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:26,890
我们有最好的仪器与最顶尖的科研人员
We've got the best equipment and the best minds

86
00:03:26,890 --> 00:03:28,240
一起在努力着呢
all working on it.

87
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,100
还好  感觉他把场救回来了
Okay, sounds like he's back on track.

88
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:32,770
虽然有时候我会觉得...
Although, some days I'm, like, ugh...

89
00:03:32,770 --> 00:03:34,680
我们花了好多好多钱啊
we've spent so much money.

90
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:38,910
怎么屁都没找到  我们是在干嘛啊
Why haven't we found anything? What are we doing?

91
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:43,980
哎妈
Oh, boy.

92
00:03:47,490 --> 00:03:48,700
莱纳德来了
There's Leonard.

93
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,530
估计他今天很不好过
I'll bet he's having a rough day.

94
00:03:50,530 --> 00:03:52,190
我们尽量表达支持吧
Let's just try to be supportive.

95
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:53,460
支持他个鬼
Supportive?

96
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:55,470
他公开诋毁了我一生挚爱
He publicly maligned the love of my life,

97
00:03:55,470 --> 00:03:57,640
物理女士
Lady Physics.

98
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:02,340
这挚爱最好别让你的未婚妻女士知道
You might not want to mention that to Lady Fiancee.

99
00:04:02,710 --> 00:04:03,290
大家好
Hey, guys.

100
00:04:03,290 --> 00:04:04,960
今天好吗
Hey, how's it going?

101
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,400
怎么  你有什么话想说吗
What? You got something to say?

102
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,840
我刚才已经说了啊
I think I just said it.

103
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:15,460
口不一
P-f-f.

104
00:04:16,350 --> 00:04:17,900
呸
Pff!

105
00:04:20,210 --> 00:04:22,440
我当时只是实话实说啊
Look, I-I was just speaking the truth.

106
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:25,070
我们是科学家  不应该用事实说话吗
We're scientists-- isn't that what we're supposed to do?

107
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:26,820
你懂个大西瓜的事实啊
Oh, what would you know about the truth?

108
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:30,330
你还觉得《星球大战I  魅影危机》很不错呢
You thought Phantom Menace was "Not half bad."

109
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:34,090
你怎么可以泄密
I told you that in confidence!

110
00:04:34,090 --> 00:04:37,080
大家冷静  别吵架了
Okay, calm down. Everybody just cool it.

111
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:38,490
别拦着啊  要是我们运气好
No, let 'em go. If we get lucky,

112
00:04:38,490 --> 00:04:41,240
说不定他们俩能有人吵哭呢
maybe one of them will start crying.

113
00:04:41,590 --> 00:04:45,170
能不能不聊这个  像成年人一样地吃午饭
Uh, can we just drop this and have lunch like adults?

114
00:04:45,170 --> 00:04:46,960
-行  -好吧
- Fine. - Very well.

115
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,210
-莱纳德  -怎么了
- Leonard? - What?

116
00:04:50,210 --> 00:04:51,620
呸
Pff!

117
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:56,530
准备好去吃饭了吗
You ready for lunch?

118
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:58,600
马上就好
Oh, one second.

119
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:01,690
某人这里多了好多新的酷炫设备啊
Ooh, someone's got a lot of fancy new lab equipment.

120
00:05:01,690 --> 00:05:02,700
对啊
I know.

121
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:05,050
大学给我的研究投了好多钱呢
The university has been throwing money at my study.

122
00:05:05,050 --> 00:05:05,640
运气好的话
With any luck,

123
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:08,480
以后说不定能有脑疾病用我名字为名呢
there'll be a brain disease with my name on it.

124
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:10,180
两指交叉为你祈祷
Fingers crossed.

125
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:12,960
讽刺的是  如果你患上了福勒瘫
Which is ironic, because if you had Fowler's palsy,

126
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:16,080
你的手将无法两指交叉
you wouldn't be able to cross your fingers.

127
00:05:16,970 --> 00:05:18,670
我很意外谢尔顿居然不来这里
I'm surprised Sheldon's not up here playing

128
00:05:18,670 --> 00:05:20,270
玩你的新玩具
with all your new toys.

129
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:22,190
其实我还没告诉他呢
Actually, I haven't told him about it.

130
00:05:22,190 --> 00:05:24,250
我们这边获得的经费比物理那边多太多
We've been getting so much more funding than physics,

131
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:25,970
他对此略为敏感
he's been a little sensitive.

132
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:28,610
所以你就对他隐瞒了你的成功吗
So you're just gonna hide your success from him?

133
00:05:28,610 --> 00:05:29,850
我知道不好
I know.

134
00:05:29,850 --> 00:05:32,130
-我是不是太坏了  -不会啊
- Am I terrible? - No.

135
00:05:32,130 --> 00:05:34,610
我也这么做
I do that, too.

136
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:38,020
美国普通城市

137
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:38,020
不然他怎么会以为我的公司年会在博伊西
How he thought my company retreat was in Boise?

138
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,330
著名度假海岛

139
00:05:38,020 --> 00:05:40,330
其实在塔希提岛
It was in Tahiti.

140
00:05:40,990 --> 00:05:42,080
那我就松一口气了
That's such a relief.

141
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:45,030
我内心曾隐隐觉得这样对谢尔顿有失公允
I mean, part of me was worried I was being unfair to Sheldon.

142
00:05:45,030 --> 00:05:47,390
将你的恻隐之心藏起来
Take that part of yourself and hide it away.

143
00:05:47,390 --> 00:05:49,250
就像我藏起我去年
Just like I did with last year's bonus check

144
00:05:49,250 --> 00:05:51,630
"并没发"的奖金支票
that I "didn't get."

145
00:05:56,210 --> 00:05:57,450
戴维斯女士  你有事找我吗
Ms. Davis, you wanted to see me?

146
00:05:57,450 --> 00:06:00,410
是的  霍夫斯塔德博士  快进来
Yes, Dr. Hofstadter, come on in.

147
00:06:00,410 --> 00:06:02,100
我是该坐下还是站着
Should I sit or stand?

148
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:04,290
我没被召进过主任办公室  不懂规矩
I'm not used to being called into the dean's office.

149
00:06:04,290 --> 00:06:06,140
请坐
Please, sit.

150
00:06:06,830 --> 00:06:08,530
不得不说  还真是有点紧张啊
I have to say I'm a little nervous.

151
00:06:08,530 --> 00:06:10,520
应该的
You should be.

152
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:13,280
我知道我搞砸了
Look, I know I screwed up,

153
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:15,340
但就是一次访谈而已
but it was only one interview.

154
00:06:15,340 --> 00:06:17,380
能对学校造成多大的损害呢
How much damage could it have caused?

155
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:19,520
你想听我念念收到的邮件吗
Would you like for me to read you the e-mails

156
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,990
学校的捐助者们都在问如果物理是条死路
from donors asking why are they giving us money

157
00:06:21,990 --> 00:06:23,820
那给咱们捐钱的意义何在
if physics is a dead end?

158
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:25,440
我可没说物理是条死路
I didn't say it was a dead end.

159
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:28,300
我只是说我担心可能会这样
I just said that I was worried it might be.

160
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:30,360
那如果我说我担心
So if I just said I was worried

161
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,980
你可能下周就要失业了
you might not have a job next week,

162
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:34,960
你感觉怎么样
how would you feel?

163
00:06:35,550 --> 00:06:39,350
头晕  还好你让我先坐下
Light-headed, and glad you asked me to sit down.

164
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:41,180
好吧  你就说我该怎么做吧
Okay, just tell me what I can do.

165
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:42,770
我要你发表一份声明
I'm gonna need you to make a statement

166
00:06:42,770 --> 00:06:45,450
说自己言论有失  并且你坚信
saying that you misspoke, and that you're confident

167
00:06:45,450 --> 00:06:49,230
物理学界即将迎来一个重大突破
the physics community is close to a major breakthrough.

168
00:06:49,230 --> 00:06:51,450
你想让我撒谎
You want me to lie.

169
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:54,820
听着  霍夫斯塔德博士  我就指望你了
Look, Dr. Hofstadter, I'm counting on you.

170
00:06:54,820 --> 00:07:00,010
我认为你是本校最聪明的物理学家
I think that you are the smartest physicist at this university.

171
00:07:00,010 --> 00:07:00,830
真的吗
Really?

172
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:04,370
瞧  撒谎一点都不难
See? Lies. They're not that hard.

173
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:15,460
感觉某人今天很用功啊
Looks like you've been busy.

174
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:16,810
是啊
Oh, I have.

175
00:07:16,810 --> 00:07:21,020
暗物质  调和广义相对论与量子力学的矛盾
Uh, dark matter, uh, reconciling gravity and quantum mechanics.

176
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:22,340
超对称性
Supersymmetry.

177
00:07:22,340 --> 00:07:25,750
我已经搞清了当今物理界最大的几个难题
I've figured out the biggest problems in physics today.

178
00:07:25,750 --> 00:07:28,200
你都解出来了吗
Wow, you solved them all?

179
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:32,390
不  我只是清楚知道了它们是最大的难题
No, I just, I figured out that they're the biggest problems.

180
00:07:33,190 --> 00:07:35,920
是因为莱纳德在电台上说的话吗
Is this about what Leonard said on the radio?

181
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:36,930
当然不是
Absolutely not.

182
00:07:36,930 --> 00:07:38,540
我也不想谈论莱纳德
And I do not want to talk about Leonard.

